{"documentation":"forkProducer makes a channel in s and runs work with it as a task of s,\nclosing the channel when work returns, so receivers' loops end. (If\nwork panics, s is cancelled, which stops them too.) A producer written\nas a named function can stop with out.send(s, x)? when the channel is\nclosed or s is cancelled.","schema_version":1,"position":{"file":"main.bork","line":13,"column":9},"type":"(Scope, Int, (Channel[Int]) =\u003e (Ok | Closed | Cancelled)) uses state =\u003e Channel[Int]","definition":{"file":"prelude/concurrency.bork","line":260,"column":1},"methods":[],"facts":[],"belongs_to":["scope s"],"callable":{"named_arguments":true,"parameter_names_are_api":true,"parameters":[{"name":"s","type":"Scope"},{"name":"capacity","type":"Int"},{"name":"work","type":"(Channel[Int]) =\u003e (Ok | Closed | Cancelled)"}]}}
